Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd938x/wcd939x: a failed zdet ramp is a floating reading

When the impedance ramp does not complete, the measurement returned
without writing a result. wcd938x then used an uninitialised value and
wcd939x a 0, which reads as a short: headphones could be classed as mono
or as a lineout depending on what was on the stack. Report the failed ramp
as floating impedance, which both callers already treat as no usable
reading.

---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd938x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd938x.c
@@ -2097,6 +2097,8 @@
 	if (!c1 || !x1) {
 		dev_err(component->dev, "Impedance detect ramp error, c1=%d, x1=0x%x\n",
 			c1, x1);
+		/* no reading is not 0 ohm */
+		*zdet = WCD938X_ZDET_FLOATING_IMPEDANCE;
 		goto ramp_down;
 	}
 	d1 = d1_a[c1];
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
@@ -2337,6 +2337,8 @@
 		dev_dbg(component->dev,
 			"%s: Impedance detect ramp error, c1=%d, x1=0x%x\n",
 			__func__, c1, x1);
+		/* no reading is not 0 ohm */
+		*zdet = WCD939X_ZDET_FLOATING_IMPEDANCE;
 		goto ramp_down;
 	}
 
